Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 01:16:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Confirm threaded SQLite close before preparing a replacement

Reserve the storage identity before the WAL scan and carry it through SQLite close. Queue CLOSED before releasing the reservation. A replacement tree waits for every connection in the previous tree, including retained facets.

Keep the proof when reset has closed SQLite and failed to reopen it. A close that SQLite cannot confirm keeps that identity fenced for this generation and rejects waiting and new opens. Report the affected identities and tag the pre-execution refusal for the node.

Exercise retained connections, the cross-thread CLOSED/OPEN order, abandoned reservations, WAL channel shutdown, reset failure, and a BUSY close with a controlled peer.

